d 'CAUSALIMPACT': module to evaluate the Causal impact of an intervention on a time series using a Bayesian structural time-series model
d
d	 causalimpact estimates the causal effect of a designed
d intervention on a time series, using the Bayesian structural	 
d time-series (BSTS) approach of Brodersen, Gallusser, Koehler,
d Remy and Scott (2015). It is a faithful Stata implementation of  
d  the R package CausalImpact 1.4.1
d (github.com/google/CausalImpact), against which it has been
d verified on shared data; see help    causalimpact rcheck.    The
d idea is a generalisation of difference-in-differences to the
d time-series setting. A state-space model is fitted to the   
d response over the pre-intervention period only, using a set of
d control series that were not themselves affected by the   
d intervention. The fitted model is then used to predict what the
d response would have been over the post-intervention period had   
d the intervention not taken place. That prediction is the
d counterfactual; the difference between the observed response and
d the	 counterfactual is the causal effect. 
d
d KW: causal effect
d KW: counterfactual
d KW: tiem series
d KW: intervention
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260805
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
